diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..79e407d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,37 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools
+
+The site exposes client-side tools through [WebMCP](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/).
+In a compatible browser and secure context, agents discover these tools through
+the browser's tool registry. Unsupported browsers retain the normal UI.
+
+Tools are registered using the React `use-webmcp-tool` integration, which feature
+detects the API and aborts registrations when Astro unmounts the islands during
+navigation. Network tools forward the execution's cancellation signal and return
+diagnostic errors for failed requests.
+
+| Tools | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | Search titles and summaries; return matching articles and deployment-relative URLs. |
+| `get_reading_list` | Return the current session's saved articles. |
+| `open_search`, `open_reading_list` | Open the corresponding form. |
+| `get_current_article` | Read the displayed article's title, summary, body, slug, and URL; return an error on other pages. |
+| `get_coffee_brew`, `get_tide_levels`, `get_plant_stats` | Request the existing article utility APIs. |
+| `get_article_popularity` | Request popularity using an article slug as `id`. |
+
+The opened flyouts expose declarative forms with `toolname`, `tooldescription`,
+and `toolautosubmit`: `search_articles_form`, `view_reading_list_form`, and
+`remove_saved_<slug>`. Article pages expose `toggle_bookmark_<slug>`.
+These low-impact forms use native named controls and return results through
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()` after updating the UI. Search remains live while typing.
+Bookmark changes notify other mounted reading-list controls.
+
+The coffee, tide, and plant endpoints are existing DevTools debugging demos.
+Tools preserve their behavior and surface HTTP failures; they do not repair the
+deliberate server errors or create the plant demo's oversized cookies.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for the client action checks (Node 22.13+), and `pnpm build`
+for production compilation. Neither requires starting a server.
